meta {
  name: VC - File Upload - URL Response
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/vc?response_mode=url
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  response_mode: url
}

body:multipart-form {
  input_audio: @file(./test-files/sample-recording.wav)
  target_voice_source: test_voices/linda_johnson_02.mp3
  chunk_sec: 60
  overlap_sec: 0.1
  export_formats: wav,mp3
  disable_watermark: true
}

docs {
  # Voice Conversion - File Upload with URL Response
  
  Upload audio file and receive JSON response with file URLs.
  
  ## Workflow
  1. Client uploads audio file
  2. Server processes voice conversion
  3. Server returns JSON with file information
  4. Client can download files using URLs
  
  ## Response Format
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "output_files": [
      {
        "format": "wav",
        "filename": "vc_2025-06-22_143045_789_chunk60_overlap0.1_voicespeaker2.wav",
        "url": "/outputs/vc_2025-06-22_143045_789_chunk60_overlap0.1_voicespeaker2.wav",
        "path": "/full/path/to/outputs/..."
      },
      {
        "format": "mp3",
        "filename": "vc_2025-06-22_143045_789_chunk60_overlap0.1_voicespeaker2.mp3",
        "url": "/outputs/vc_2025-06-22_143045_789_chunk60_overlap0.1_voicespeaker2.mp3",
        "path": "/full/path/to/outputs/..."
      }
    ],
    "processing_time_seconds": 8.7,
    "message": "Voice conversion completed successfully",
    "timestamp": "2025-06-22T14:30:45Z"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Web apps where user uploads audio for conversion
  - Mobile apps with audio recording
  - Forms with file upload fields
  - Systems needing upload and process workflow
  
  ## Advantages
  - No pre-staging required
  - Single request for upload and conversion
  - Get metadata before downloading
  - Easy to integrate with web forms
  
  ## Limitations
  - 100MB file size limit
  - Longer processing time (upload + conversion)
  - Not suitable for very large files
}
